---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="PeptiBloom"
  description="PeptiBloom is building a public scientific research library designed around evidence, transparency, traceability and visible uncertainty."
>
  <section class="section section--hero">
    <div class="site-frame hero">
      <div class="hero__copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">Scientific Research Library</p>
        <h1>Know what we know.<br />Know what we don’t.</h1>
        <p class="hero__lead">
          PeptiBloom is building a public scientific research library designed to make evidence,
          uncertainty, provenance and open questions easier to inspect.
        </p>
        <div class="hero__actions" aria-label="Primary actions">
          <a class="button button--primary" href="/library/">Explore the library</a>
          <a class="editorial-link" href="/methodology/">Read our methodology <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="hero__visual" aria-hidden="true">
        <div class="evidence-halo">
          <span class="evidence-halo__ring evidence-halo__ring--outer"></span>
          <span class="evidence-halo__ring evidence-halo__ring--middle"></span>
          <span class="evidence-halo__ring evidence-halo__ring--inner"></span>
          <span class="evidence-halo__node evidence-halo__node--one"></span>
          <span class="evidence-halo__node evidence-halo__node--two"></span>
          <span class="evidence-halo__node evidence-halo__node--three"></span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--quiet" aria-labelledby="purpose-title">
    <div class="site-frame">
      <div class="section-heading reading-column">
        <p class="eyebrow">Purpose</p>
        <h2 id="purpose-title">Scientific information should show its limits as clearly as its conclusions.</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="principle-grid">
        <article class="principle">
          <p class="principle__index">01</p>
          <h3>Evidence</h3>
          <p>Separate what is supported from what is theoretical, contradictory or anecdotal.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="principle">
          <p class="principle__index">02</p>
          <h3>Transparency</h3>
          <p>Make ownership, limitations and unresolved questions visible rather than hiding them behind certainty.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="principle">
          <p class="principle__index">03</p>
          <h3>Traceability</h3>
          <p>Keep the path back to sources and provenance inspectable.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="library-title">
    <div class="site-frame feature-layout">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Scientific Library</p>
        <h2 id="library-title">A library before a catalogue.</h2>
        <p class="section-lead">
          Scientific entries are published to inform research, not to fill a product grid. PeptiBloom’s
          public library is structured around what the evidence can support, where it conflicts and what
          still remains unanswered.
        </p>
        <a class="editorial-link" href="/library/">Enter the Scientific Library <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      </div>

      <aside class="editorial-surface" aria-labelledby="publication-standard-title">
        <p class="surface-kicker">Publication standard</p>
        <h3 id="publication-standard-title">No scientific content just to fill space.</h3>
        <p>
          Production scientific content must complete the approved review path before it appears as a
          library entry. Until then, the web does not invent studies, claims, evidence levels or compounds.
        </p>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--soft" aria-labelledby="method-title">
    <div class="site-frame">
      <div class="section-heading reading-column">
        <p class="eyebrow">Methodology</p>
        <h2 id="method-title">A visible path from source to interpretation.</h2>
      </div>

      <ol class="method-steps" aria-label="Editorial research process">
        <li>
          <span>01</span>
          <h3>Source</h3>
          <p>Start with inspectable provenance rather than unsupported summaries.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span>02</span>
          <h3>Review</h3>
          <p>Separate evidence from hypothesis, contradiction and anecdotal experience.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span>03</span>
          <h3>Interpretation</h3>
          <p>Describe what the available evidence supports without manufacturing certainty.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span>04</span>
          <h3>Traceability</h3>
          <p>Preserve a clear route back to the underlying sources and limitations.</p>
        </li>
      </ol>

      <a class="editorial-link" href="/methodology/">How PeptiBloom handles evidence <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="uncertainty-title">
    <div class="site-frame uncertainty-layout">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">Designed uncertainty</p>
        <h2 id="uncertainty-title">The unknown belongs on the page.</h2>
        <p>
          A useful scientific library should make it easy to see both the support for a conclusion and the
          limits around it.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="uncertainty-pair">
        <article class="uncertainty-panel">
          <p class="surface-kicker">What the evidence supports</p>
          <h3>Conclusions with visible provenance.</h3>
          <p>Supported findings should be understandable in context and traceable to their sources.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="uncertainty-panel uncertainty-panel--open">
          <p class="surface-kicker">What remains uncertain</p>
          <h3>Contradictions and gaps are findings too.</h3>
          <p>Missing evidence, disagreement and unanswered questions should remain visible rather than being normalised into certainty.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--transparency" aria-labelledby="transparency-title">
    <div class="site-frame transparency-band">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Transparency</p>
        <h2 id="transparency-title">Ownership should be visible.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="reading-column">
        <p>
          The Scientific Library is a PeptiBloom initiative, and that ownership is shown explicitly.
          Scientific information remains structurally distinguishable from commercial information.
        </p>
        <a class="editorial-link" href="/about/">About PeptiBloom and this library <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
